# ez2vr native runtime graph -- Entropy: Zero 2 on Quest (arm64-v8a)
#
# WHAT THIS FILE IS
# The declaration of every native library the EZ2 engine needs at runtime. It is
# the source of truth for two things:
#
#   1. tools/stage-engine-libs.gradle (task :app:stageEngineLibs) copies exactly
#      these names into app/src/main/jniLibs/arm64-v8a/ and FAILS if any of them
#      cannot be found, naming what is missing.
#   2. EZ2EngineActivity.verifyNativeGraph() parses it on device and checks each
#      name against the libs actually installed in the APK, so the launcher
#      fails loudly on a partial engine instead of dying in dlopen.
#
# WHY IT EXISTS AT ALL, GIVEN NOTHING READS IT
# The engine logs SOURCEVR_RUNTIME_GRAPH (the staged copy's path) at
# launcher/android/main.cpp:249 and then ignores it -- there is no .load parser
# in the engine. The engine loads liblauncher.so via System.loadLibrary and the
# rest by ordinary dlopen out of the APK's extracted native lib dir. So an
# earlier version of this file was a bare token that only had to EXIST to get
# EZ2EngineActivity.hasNativeGraph() past its gate, which made that check
# impossible to fail. Making it a real manifest costs nothing and turns it into
# a check that means something. Keep the format deliberately boring: one library
# name per line, '#' comments, blank lines ignored.
#
# THE SET (31 libraries)
# 27 from the engine build tree (`find build -name '*.so'`), which is the same
# collection the proven EZ1 pipeline packages, plus four more the build cannot
# produce on its own. The engine dlopen()s only three of these by name
# (libengine.so, libinputsystem.so, liblauncher.so); the rest are resolved by the
# engine's own module search over the native lib dir, so all of them must ship.
#
#   libSDL2.so          the engine's platform layer, built by the tree
#   libopenxr_loader.so Khronos loader; the tree's copy is vendored under
#                       external/openxr, CI fetches the same lib from the AAR
#   libc++_shared.so    NDK r20b arm64 runtime, required because the engine is
#                       built -stdlib=libc++ and links it dynamically
#   libhidapi.so        built from android/native/hidapi_stub.c (see the Gradle
#                       task; there is no other hidapi for this platform)
#
# IF YOU EDIT THIS: re-run :app:stageEngineLibs, which cross-checks the manifest
# against the engine build tree and reports drift. Adding a library to the
# engine build means adding it here too, or the launcher will refuse to start
# with a name it does not recognise.

# --- engine build tree (27) ---
libclient.so
libdatacache.so
libengine.so
libfilesystem_stdio.so
libGameUI.so
libinputsystem.so
liblauncher.so
libmaterialsystem.so
libscenefilecache.so
libserver.so
libServerBrowser.so
libshaderapidx9.so
libsoundemittersystem.so
libsourcevr.so
libstdshader_dx9.so
libsteam_api.so
libstudiorender.so
libtier0.so
libtogl.so
libvaudio_minimp3.so
libvaudio_opus.so
libvgui2.so
libvguimatsurface.so
libvideo_services.so
libvphysics.so
libvstdlib.so
libvtex_dll.so

# --- supplied from outside the build tree (4) ---
libSDL2.so
libopenxr_loader.so
libc++_shared.so
libhidapi.so
